Where an account starts
01-accounts-and-security
Chooses what a person sees when they sign on to this account, and when they type logto to enter it: the home screen (menu), the ordinary command prompt (terminal), or whatever the system default says.
It confines nobody on its own. The Terminal tile on the home screen still gives the command prompt unless you turn that tile off for the account.
The change reaches the person at their next sign-on. The command it runs is modify.account with start-menu, start-terminal or start-default.
